    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Differential diagnosis of gestational trophoblastic neoplasms</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Annie Nga-Yin Cheung",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 730.75pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Diagnostic features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Gestational choriocarcinoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Non-gestational choriocarcinoma of germ cell origin</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Non-gestational somatic carcinoma with trophoblastic differentiation and ectopic hCG production.</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>PSTT</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>ETT</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Trophoblastic proliferations in early gestation or complete mole</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>EPS and PSN</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Age</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Reproductive age (average: 29&ndash;31&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Commonly occurs in children and young adults</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uterine cases are more common in postmenopausal women</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">20&ndash;63&nbsp;years (average: 30&ndash;32&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">15&ndash;48&nbsp;years (average: 36&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Reproductive age</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Reproductive age</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Antecedent pregnancy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Term pregnancy, complete hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unrelated to a prior gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unrelated to a prior gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Term pregnancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Term pregnancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early pregnancy, complete hydatidiform mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Early or term pregnancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Interval time from index gestation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A few months to 14&nbsp;years (average: 2&nbsp;months after term pregnancy, 13&nbsp;months after complete mole)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">2&nbsp;weeks to 17&nbsp;years (median: 12&ndash;18&nbsp;months)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">1&ndash;25&nbsp;years (average: 6.2&nbsp;years)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Clinical presentation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vaginal bleeding, persistent GTD</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">An adnexal mass, lower abdominal pain mimicking an ectopic pregnancy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vaginal bleeding or symptoms of extrauterine bleeding</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Missed abortion, amenorrhoea</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Vaginal bleeding</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often asymptomatic</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pretreatment hCG (mIU/mL)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&gt;&nbsp;10&times;10<sup>3</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;1&times;10<sup>3</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&lt;&nbsp;3&times;10<sup>3</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Not increased</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Gross appearance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumscribed or invasive haemorrhagic masses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumscribed or invasive haemorrhagic masses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Circumscribed or invasive haemorrhagic masses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Expansile to infiltrative solid mass</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Expansile solid mass</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absence of mass lesion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absence of mass lesion</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tumour location</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Corpus</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Ovary, extragonadal sites along the midline, and rarely the fallopian tube</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Corpus, extrauterine sites</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Corpus</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cervix, lower uterine segment, corpus</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Endometrium or ectopic sites</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Endometrium, occasionally cervix or fallopian tube</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histopathology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infiltrative tumour border; extensive haemorrhage and necrosis; characteristic bilaminar pattern with mononuclear trophoblasts rimmed by multinucleated syncytiotrophoblasts; marked cytological atypia noted</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infiltrative tumour border; extensive haemorrhage and necrosis; characteristic bilaminar pattern with mononuclear trophoblasts rimmed by multinucleated syncytiotrophoblasts; marked cytological atypia noted; may coexist with germ cell tumour of other types; thorough sampling important</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infiltrative tumour border; presence of carcinoma of discernible differentiation; thorough sampling important; marked cytological atypia usually present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Infiltrative tumour border; sheets; tumour cells replacing vascular wall; tumour cells splitting myometrial smooth muscle fibres at tumour periphery; moderate to marked cytological atypia present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pushing tumour border; sheets, nests, and cords; geographical necrosis; deposition of hyaline-like materials; colonizing mucosal surface epithelium; moderate to marked cytological atypia present; presence of nearby decidualized stromal cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absence of atypia in trophoblasts of early gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well circumscribed, with absence of overtly malignant nuclear morphology</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tumour cells</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Villous intermediate trophoblast, syncytiotrophoblast, and cytotrophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Villous intermediate trophoblast, syncytiotrophoblast, and cytotrophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Poorly differentiated carcinoma with scattered hCG-producing multinucleated giant cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Implantation site&ndash;type intermediate trophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Chorionic-type intermediate trophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Implantation site&ndash;type intermediate trophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Chorionic-type intermediate trophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>IHC</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive for hCG, hPL, HSD3B1, and SALL4 in syncytiotrophoblast; Ki-67 proliferation index &gt;&nbsp;90%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive for hCG, hPL, HSD3B1, and SALL4 in syncytiotrophoblast</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Positive for hCG in multinucleated cells</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive for hPL and MCAM; scattered multinuclear cells positive for hCG; Ki-67 proliferation index of 5&ndash;10%; negative for SALL4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive for p63; rare individual cells positive for hPL and MCAM; Ki-67 proliferation index &gt;&nbsp;10%; negative for SALL4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Diffusely positive for hPL and MCAM; scattered multinuclear cells positive for hCG; Ki-67 proliferation index &lt;&nbsp;5%; negative for SALL4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PSN is positive for p63 and often negative for hPL, MCAM, and SALL4; Ki-67 proliferation index is &lt;&nbsp;5%&nbsp;for PSN and 5&ndash;10% for APSN; EPS is positive for hPL and MCAM, negative for p63; Ki-67 proliferation index in EPS is low (&lt; 1%) and can be &gt; 5%&nbsp;for EPS associated with complete mole</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.4pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"119\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>STR DNA genotyping</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Presence of unique paternal alleles of the index gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 113.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"151\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Biallelic (germ cell) pattern<sup>a</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 88.85pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"118\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Biallelic (somatic cell) pattern</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"107\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Presence of unique paternal alleles of the index gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 75.35pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"100\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Presence of unique paternal alleles of the index gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.65pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"113\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Monospermic or dispermic allelic pattern</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 85.15pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Presence of unique paternal alleles of the index gestation</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">APSN, atypical placental site nodule; EPS, exaggerated placental site; ETT, epithelioid trophoblastic tumour; GTD, gestational trophoblastic disease; IHC, immunohistochemistry; PSN, placental site nodule/plaque; PSTT, placental site trophoblastic tumour; STR, short tandem repeat.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Possible homozygous pattern in a choriocarcinoma arising from a germ cell after meiosis.</p>",
